    <section id="faq" style="margin-top: 4rem;">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <h3>What is the best INDmoney alternative that doesn't read your emails?</h3>
      <p>Arthavi is the best privacy-first INDmoney alternative. Unlike INDmoney which requests full Gmail read access to scrape investment emails, Arthavi imports your portfolio through direct CAS PDF upload — no email access, no broker passwords, and no data selling to lenders or insurance companies.</p>

      <h3>Does INDmoney really read your emails?</h3>
      <p>Yes. INDmoney requests Gmail OAuth permissions to read your emails for automatic portfolio tracking. This means the app has access to all your investment confirmation emails, bank statements, and other sensitive financial correspondence. Arthavi never requests email access.</p>

      <h3>Does INDmoney sell your data to lenders?</h3>
      <p>INDmoney monetizes through cross-selling financial products including loans, credit cards, and insurance. Users frequently report receiving marketing calls after signing up. Arthavi has zero cross-selling, zero data monetization, and does not even collect phone numbers during signup.</p>

      <h3>Is Arthavi better than INDmoney for portfolio tracking?</h3>
      <p>For pure portfolio tracking without cross-selling or privacy trade-offs, yes. Arthavi focuses exclusively on accurate portfolio analytics with CAS import, family portfolios, XIRR, and AI analysis. INDmoney is a super-app that bundles tracking with lending, insurance, and US stocks.</p>

      <h3>Can I track my complete portfolio on Arthavi without linking broker accounts?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Arthavi tracks mutual funds via CAS PDF import and stocks via manual entry or CSV upload. You never need to link Zerodha, Groww, or any broker account. Your portfolio data stays fully under your control.</p>
    </section>

